# Project-local npm config.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# This machine's DSH workspace runs under a filesystem sandbox: the default npm
# cache directory (`C:\Users\RUNIC\scoop\persist\nodejs\cache`) sits OUTSIDE the
# writable workspace, so npm fails with
#
#   npm error code EPERM
#   npm error syscall open
#   npm error path C:\Users\RUNIC\scoop\persist\nodejs\cache\_cacache\tmp\***
#
# even though the registry itself is perfectly reachable (`npm ping` → PONG).
# Pointing the cache at a directory INSIDE this workspace keeps installs working
# without touching any global npm configuration.
#
# Verified: `npm view tsdown version --cache W:\dsh-plugins\dsh-rtt-debug\.npm-cache`
#           → 0.23.0
#
# NOTE: `store-dir` is a pnpm-only key — npm warns about it, so it lives in
# .npmrc.pnpm instead (pnpm reads it from there via the store-dir setting below).
# Keeping the unwanted key out of this file is what silences the npm warning.

cache=.npm-cache

# Packages are fetched from the public registry (default). No proxy is needed;
# `npm config get proxy` / `https-proxy` are both null on this machine.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
